The Verdict
If viewed as an operating philosophy for building local-first, self-healing cognitive architectures, it works remarkably well. It gives you a clean lens to strip out syntactic noise, focus on relational invariants, and maintain lean system states.
If viewed as a zero-touch continuous runtime engine, its success depends entirely on how rigorously you construct the ground-truth validators (the test suites that enforce invariants when translating between abstract graphs and concrete implementations).
